@startuml 02_sequence_abr
title ABR switching under the tc bandwidth steps (hls.js)
skinparam shadowing false
participant "tc_steps.sh" as TC
participant "Nginx / Wi-Fi link" as NET
participant "hls.js loader" as LD
participant "EWMA estimator\n(fast 3 s, slow 9 s)" as EST
participant "ABR controller" as ABR
participant "Video element" as VID
== start ==
LD -> NET : GET master.m3u8
NET --> LD : 3 levels (BANDWIDTH 2891 / 1461 / 691 kbit/s)
LD -> ABR : first level = 720p
== steady state: one segment per second ==
loop every segment (1 s)
  LD -> NET : GET 720p/segN.m4s
  NET --> LD : 2.6 Mbit in about 0.13 s
  LD -> EST : sample(size / load time, weight = load time)
  EST --> ABR : estimate = min(fast, slow)
  ABR -> ABR : up: 0.7 x est >= BANDWIDTH\ndown: 0.95 x est >= BANDWIDTH
end
== link drops to 2.5 Mbit/s ==
TC -> NET : tbf rate 2500kbit
LD -> NET : GET 720p/segN+1.m4s
NET --> LD : slower than real time (~1.1 s per 1 s of video)
LD -> EST : low sample, fast average drops
EST --> ABR : estimate < 3043 kbit/s
ABR --> LD : next level = 540p (switch after 6-9 s measured)
LD -> VID : append 540p fragments (buffer stays > 1.4 s)
== link recovers ==
TC -> NET : tbf rate 5mbit
LD -> EST : high samples, slow average rises
note over EST, ABR : up-switch is conservative:\n720p needs est >= 4130 kbit/s,\nmeasured delay about 65 s
EST --> ABR : estimate grows
ABR --> LD : next level = 720p
@enduml
